Aldus
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/the_hermitage]

He works the vine a while longer. You wonder if perhaps he didn't hear you.

"Tell me something, while I have you. A man eats stolen bread. Another man starves beside the bread. Which of them is the thief?"

choices:

* "The one who ate it." = Culpability follows the act.
    He nods once, as if you had answered a different question.

    "And when the bread is gone," he says, "and only the starving remain. What then?"

    He does not wait for an answer. His hand goes back to the soil.
    +open Garden

* "The one who let him eat." = The bystander is complicit.
    He reaches into the dirt and sets a small pebble on the path between you.

    "It was not here. Now it is. Soon it will be somewhere else."

    He does not look up. His hand returns to the vines.
    +open Garden

* "Neither. The man who baked the bread." = The question presumes a world that did not feed them both.
    Something at the corner of his mouth moves. It is not quite a smile.

    "You are not the first to answer that way."
    +open Garden

* "I have no answer." = Decline the question.
    He is quiet for a long time. You think he may have forgotten you.

    "Good," he says at last, mildly. Whether you have passed a small test or failed one is not clear.
    +open Garden
